==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|lesa|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|lesaną|lang=gem-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɛːsa/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɛːsa|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|las|lásu|lesið}}

# {{transitive|with accusative|lang=is}} to [[gather]], [[pick]] (usually berries, etc.)
# {{ambitransitive|with accusative|lang=is}} to [[read]]
#: ''Ég er að '''lesa''' bók um forritun.''
#:: I'm '''reading''' a book on programming.
#: ''Þá var bréfið '''lesið''' upphátt fyrir allan bekkinn.''
#:: The letter was then '''read''' aloud in front of the entire class.
# {{ambitransitive|with accusative|lang=is}} to [[study]]

====Derived terms====
* [[les-]] ([[read-only]])
* [[lesblinda]]
* [[lesblindur]]
* [[lesa fyrir bréf]] (to dictate a letter)
* [[lesa saman]] (to compare)
* [[lesa spjaldanna á milli]]
* [[lesa upp]] (to recite)
* [[lesa upphátt]] (to read aloud)

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|lestur}}

