==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|lesaną|lang=gem-pro}}. The sense “read” is derived from West Germanic (Old Saxon or Old High German), calquing {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|lego|legō|gather, read|lang=la}}; for reading the Germanic [[rune]]s, which were in use before the adoption of the Latin alphabet, the usual verb had been {{term|ráða|lang=non}} (same as English {{term|read|lang=en}}).

===Verb===
{{head|non|verb}}

# to [[gather]], [[pick]]
# to [[read]]

====Descendants====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|lesa}}
* Faroese: {{l|fo|lesa}}
* Norwegian: {{l|no|lese}}
* Danish: {{l|da|læse}}
* Swedish: {{l|sv|läsa}}

